sible user input going into a `path.join` or `path.resolve` function. This could possibly lead to a path traversal vulnerability,  where the attacker can access arbitrary files stored in the file system. Instead, be sure to sanitize or validate user input first.\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"cwe_id\": \"CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')\",\n      \"affected_system\": \"/tmp/aegis-0d35443a-6263-4deb-94e2-6ede6a63c43d/repo/src/utils/sandbox.ts\",\n      \"affected_component\": \"/tmp/aegis-0d35443a-6263-4deb-94e2-6ede6a63c43d/repo/src/utils/sandbox.ts:92\",\n      \"evidence\": \"requires login\",\n      \"remediation\": \"Review and fix the security issue at /tmp/aegis-0d35443a-6263-4deb-94e2-6ede6a63c43d/repo/src/utils/sandbox.ts:92\",\n      \"references\": [\n        \"https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Path_Traversal\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total_findings\": 7,\n    \"critical\": 0,\n    \"high\": 1,\n    \"medium\": 5,\n    \"low\": 1\n  }\n}"}]},"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2}

